You have dry eye caused mainly by meibomian gland dysfunction in both eyes. Along the eyelid margins are tiny oil glands that should release a thin layer of oil with each blink. That oil slows tear evaporation and keeps the surface of the eye comfortable.\
\
In your case, the oil has become thicker and more waxy, so it does not flow or spread properly. Screen time often makes this worse because we blink less often and less completely when reading or focusing on digital devices. As a result, tears evaporate too quickly. This can cause burning, stinging, fluctuating vision, a tired feeling, watering, and the urge to rub the eyes.\
\
